---
Manage data-models within a project.

A data-model (called "ontology" in DSP-API) defines the schema for a project's resources: the resource-types, their fields, and value-types.

Usage: dsp vre data-model [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list       List all data-models in a project
  describe   Describe a single data-model
  structure  Show the relations (links + inheritance) between a data-model's resource-types
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -v, --verbose...
          Increase log verbosity (-v=info, -vv=debug, -vvv=trace). RUST_LOG overrides

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
